I was born in 1934 one of a pair of  twins Miriam and I were the certain  ports children in the family we lived in  a very small village in Transylvania  Romania  [Music]  [Applause]  we got them from the cattle car people  were selected to live or to die people  crying pushing shoving  dogs barking trying to make some sense  of that place and I actually turned  around in trying to figure out what is  it I've never seen a place like that  before and as I turned around I realized  that my father and my two older sisters  were gone never saw them again we were  holding on to mother for dear life and  not he was running in the middle of that  selection platform yelling in German  twins twins he noticed us and demanded  to know if we were twins my mother asked  is that good and the Nazi said yes my  mother said yes at that moment another  Nazi came pulled my mother to the right  we were pulled to the left we were  crying she was crying and alive I  remember is seeing my mother's arms  stretched out in this parish she was  pulled away I never even said goodbye to  her but I did not understand that this  would be the last time that we would see  her and all that took 30 minutes from  the time with that done from the cattle  car and my whole family was gone  only Miriam and I were left holding  hands and cried we were Mengele twins  which we found out later on what that  meant  [Music]  Mangala would count us every morning and  he wanted to know how many guinea pigs  he had this day I was used in two types  of experiments Monday Wednesday Friday  they would put me naked in a room with  my twin sister and many other twins up  to eight hours a day they would measure  every part of my body compare it to my  twin sister and then compare it to chart  on alternate days Tuesday Thursday  Saturday they would take us to a blood  lab they would tie both of my arms to  restrict the blood flow take a lot of  blood from my left arm and give me a  minimum of five injections in the writer  the content of those injections we  didn't know then not doing now today  after one of those injections I became  very ill with a very high fever my legs  and arms were swollen and very painful I  was trembling as the August Sun was  burning my skin and I had huge red spots  covering my body the next visit is a  blood leg they didn't tie my arms  instead of that measure my fever and I  was immediately taken to the hospital  the hospital was another barrack but it  was filled with people who looked me  more dead than alive  next morning Mangala came in was four of  the doctors never ever examined me he  looked at my favorite chart and then he  declared too bad she's so young she has  only two weeks to live for the following  two weeks I have only one clear memory  crawling on the barrack floor because I  no longer could walk and crawling to  reach apposite with water at the other  end of the barrack and as I was crawling  I would fade out in and out of  consciousness telling myself I must  survive I must survive after two weeks  my favor broke and I felt immediately a  lot stronger it took me another three  weeks before my fever charge of normal  Miriam and I got back she was sitting on  the bed staring into space when I asked  her what happened to you she said I  cannot talk about it I will not talk  about it  and we didn't talk about Auschwitz until  1985  [Music]  and I asked her in 85 Miriam do you  remember when I was taken to the  hospital she said yes I said what  happened to you while I was in the  hospital she said I was under Nazi  doctors supervision 24 hours a day it  was the same two weeks that Mangala said  I would die so I said to him what  happened to you after the two weeks were  up she said she was taken back to the  labs injected with many injections that  made her feel very sick as I found out  years later and she grew up got married  in Israel expected her first child she  developed severe kidney infections that  did not respond to any antibiotic second  pregnancy in 63 the infection got so bad  that the Israeli doctor studied her and  they found out that Miriam's kidneys  never grew larger they're the size of a  ten-year-old child so I begged Miriam  that not to have any more children  because every pregnancy were the life  crisis but she had a third child and  after the search child was born her  kidneys deteriorated started to  deteriorate and by 1987 they failed at  which time I donated my left kidney I  had two kidneys and one sister so it was  an easy choice but a year later she  developed cancerous polyps in the  bladder the doctors kept asking me to  find our office files we never found our  files we never found out what was  injected into our bodies Miriam died  June 6 1993 months after Miriam died  the telephone call from a professor and  master who said he heard me speak and he  would like me to go to Boston and speak  and when I came there it would be nice  if I could bring a naughty laughter I  was stunned at such a question  and when I thought about it I remembered  that the last project that Miriam and I  worked together before she died was 1992  and for the documentary done by a German  television about the Mangala twins and  in that documentary  there was a Nazi doctor from Auschwitz  and I figured the fever of the life in  92 he might be alive in 93 so I got his  telephone number I called him and  invited him to Boston  when he told me was not going to go to  Boston but he was willing to meet with  me at his house in Germany I think then  didn't plan to ask him any of these  questions suddenly I am asking you were  in Auschwitz did you ever walk by gas  chamber did you ever go inside the gas  chamber do you know how the gas chamber  operated listen this is the nightmare  that I live with every single day of my  life and when I'm describing the  operation of the gas stream but he was  stationed outside looking through a  peephole while the gas was coming down  and people were dying then 